<area shape="poly" id="edge4" href="https://www.row2k.com/results/resultspage.cfm?UID=F58C6BF71D67F028BA2055A66A6FA063&amp;cat=1" title="NEIRA Girls Fours, Berkshire v Canterbury, Greenwich Academy, Lyme/Old Lyme, Sacred Heart			
Distance: 1300 M Conditions: Steady rain; occasional very light tailwind; flat water. Comments: Races alternated with boys&#39; races. Order of racing: 3V, 2V, 1V, 4V. Berkshire hotseated a rower from 3V to 4V. To ensure fair racing, the course was shortened from 1500 M due to aggressive weed growth in the starting area. In 3V race, GA caught a boat&#45;stopping crab just short of the finish. This would not have impacted finish order, but may have increased the margin. Kudos to cox&#39;ns in 1V and 2V for managing tight 5&#45;boat starts.
